        "original_id": "df5415e3-49c0-54b9-8076-1a58f647b6b1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Korean Jindo, Taigan\n- Organizations: United Kennel Club, Fédération Cynologique Internationale, national kennel clubs\n- Places: Kyrgyzstan\n- Concepts: dog breed recognition, sighthound breeds\n\nFacts:\n- The Korean Jindo breed was recognized by the United Kennel Club on January 1, 1998.\n- The Korean Jindo breed was recognized by the Fédération Cynologique Internationale in 2005.\n- The Taigan is a sighthound breed from Kyrgyzstan.\n- The Taigan is also known as Kyrgyzdyn Taighany and as Kyrgyzskaya Borzaya Taigan in Russian.\n- The Taigan is not recognized by the Fédération Cynologique Internationale.\n- The Taigan is recognized by a number of kennel clubs at the national level.",
